A cross between Civilization and Total War: Shogun, Oriental Empires has potential, but I can't recommend the game in its current state:
* combat needs improvement (particularly city sieges and battle formations);
* diplomacy is nearly non-existent;
* economy seems broken (markets and the like seem to cost more to maintain than they generate);
* skill trees are confusing with little information, so not clear what benefits each skill offeres or even which prerequisites are necessary to select that skill.
I want to like this game, but it's just not there yet. I realized it when I was 100 or so turns in and just got bored with everything. Nothing like the "just ... one ... more ... turn" feel of Civ or Total War. Hoping the Devs fix these issues so I can change my review.

